WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:04.421
Tell me why you're here.

00:00:04.629 --> 00:00:05.755
What are you doing in this country?

00:00:07.215 --> 00:00:08.925
This country has always been

00:00:08.925 --> 00:00:11.553
a place that people come
to find themselves,

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:14.014
and to find their dreams.

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:19.227
The stories of immigrants
coming to the United States

00:00:19.227 --> 00:00:22.355
are both incredibly unique,
but also universal.

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:30.155
Life is full of comedy and drama,

00:00:30.155 --> 00:00:33.158
and sometimes those things
live side by side.

00:00:33.158 --> 00:00:36.995
It says here you got permission
for an expedited wedding…

00:00:36.995 --> 00:00:40.165
because you are
eight months pregnant?

00:00:40.623 --> 00:00:41.374
Yes.

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:46.337
What happens when you come here
and you have a dream-

00:00:46.421 --> 00:00:48.548
This place is like a jail.

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:49.799
And that dream doesn't work out.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:55.430
Everyone struggles.

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:58.016
And sometimes success
comes in different ways.

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:01.061
All these women come into your shop,

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:03.521
you make them feel like
the best version of themselves.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:06.858
Why can’t you do that for yourself?

00:01:10.445 --> 00:01:12.530
Whether we come here or we grew up here,

00:01:13.156 --> 00:01:15.867
I think everybody can see themselves
in these stories.

00:01:18.369 --> 00:01:21.331
Before you even saw a piano,

00:01:21.331 --> 00:01:23.792
you were better than most pianists.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:28.004
This is such a beautiful portrait

00:01:28.004 --> 00:01:31.800
of the tapestry of
immigrant experiences in America.

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:34.052
This is our life now,

00:01:34.052 --> 00:01:35.261
and I love it.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:35.804
Go!

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:37.222
Ahh!

